{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation evidence — Gerrit change 1951 (Change-Id I026ad4ca58516df192a4046a3262acef7e87e90f), commit 6451d3ff02.\n\nDUPLICATE NOTE: the plan-review overlap detector flagged this ticket as `duplicates` 039b-d179-b669-4439 (classless-dainty-lamprey, confidence 0.82), which shares the title and both file-impact paths and landed the first pass as a79ed876b0. `rebar link 039b-d179-b669-4439 decagonal-indisposed-tamarin duplicates` was refused because the source ticket is closed, so the relation is recorded here instead. This change covers only the residual work that 039b left on main; it does not re-do 039b's slow-progress/read-retry repair.\n\nWINDOWS — old -> new (all test-only; production defaults byte-unchanged at 120s call / 3s grace / 2s drain / 10s low-speed window):\n- test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py, blanket autouse `_short_timeout`: REBAR_ACLI_TIMEOUT=1 + 1s grace + 1s drain, applied to the WHOLE module -> deleted. Replaced by two opt-in fixtures: `real_child` (0.2s call / 0.1s grace / 0.1s drain) for the six tests whose fake child must HANG, and `completing_child_timeout` (30s) for test_run_acli_429_retries_with_rate_limit_backoff, whose two fake children must COMPLETE. That test previously inherited the 1s ceiling as a pass condition — a latent load flake in the opposite direction, which merely shrinking a shared value would have worsened.\n- test_snapshot_fetch_stall_abort_12e4.py, `tight_stall`: REBAR_SNAPSHOT_STALL_WINDOW_SECONDS 2 -> 1 (the smallest value git's http.lowSpeedTime expresses; the sibling dribble test already proved git honors a 1s window).\n\nREMOVING REAL-TIME DEPENDENCE, not just shrinking numbers. Three reap tests assert on something the child must have finished FIRST (the grandchild pidfile, the spawn counter, the flushed partial stdout); on main that ordering held only because 1s happened to exceed interpreter startup. Every hanging fake now creates a readiness file as its last act, and a parent-side Popen wrapper polls for that file before returning the process. `_run_acli` computes `call_timeout` before the loop but measures the deadline at `communicate()`, i.e. after the wrapper returns, so the injected window is spent entirely on the hang. The PID-existence checks poll to a transition via a shared `_wait_until_gone` helper under a 30s ceiling instead of the previous 5s.\n\nWHY THESE VALUES CANNOT FLAKE ON A SLOW HOST:\n- Every fake sleeps 3600s, so a SMALLER reap window makes the timeout more certain, never less: no amount of load lets the child finish first.\n- Everything that could have raced the window is now gated on an observed file, not on elapsed time.\n- The only remaining ceilings are hang-guards a healthy run never approaches: the 10s reap guard (~25x the 0.4s injected window, kept at 10s and NOT tightened, marker `# timing: hang-guard`), the 30s readiness/PID poll ceilings, the 30s completing-child timeout, and the unchanged 60s `_GIT_TIMEOUT` in the snapshot fixture (60x its 1s window).\n- The stalled remote sends ZERO bytes, so a loaded host can delay the abort but cannot manufacture throughput above the floor; the pass condition is the failure REASON (`\"stalled\" in message`, `\"timed out after\" not in message`), never a duration.\n\nDISCRIMINATION PROOF — ten seeded defects, each RED with the expected assertion, each reverted (`git diff -- src` clean afterwards):\n- D0 terminal raise changed from AcliTimeoutError to TimeoutError -> ALL SIX reap tests RED (proves none passes vacuously).\n- D1 `_reap_process_group` replaced by `p.kill(); p.wait()` (direct child only) -> test_grandchild_process_group_reaped RED: \"grandchild PID 13172 survived the process-group reap\".\n- D2 `if retry_on_timeout and attempt < _MAX_ATTEMPTS - 1` -> `if attempt < ...` -> test_write_not_retried_on_timeout RED: \"a timed-out WRITE must not be retried\".\n- D3 same gate forced False -> test_read_retried_then_terminal RED: \"a READ should retry up to _MAX_ATTEMPTS times\".\n- D4 Popen `errors=\"replace\"` -> `\"strict\"` -> test_truncated_utf8_does_not_crash_reap_path RED: UnicodeDecodeError.\n- D5 `partial_stdout=partial_out` -> `None` -> test_partial_stdout_captured_on_timeout RED: \"assert None is not None\".\n- D6 `_check_mutation_failure` invoked on the timeout path -> test_check_mutation_failure_not_called_on_killed_child RED.\n- D7 `rl_delay = _rate_limit_backoff(...)` -> `None` -> test_run_acli_429_retries_with_rate_limit_backoff RED: \"expected one Retry-After=1 backoff, got [2]\".\n- S1 `stall_abort_args()` -> `[]` -> test_stalled_remote_aborts_on_throughput_not_the_wall_clock RED.\n- S2 floor forced to 10**9 (abort regardless of throughput = time-keyed) -> test_slow_but_progressing_remote_is_not_aborted RED: \"stalled — the remote went quiet\".\nGREEN restored after every revert.\n\nMEASUREMENTS (macOS, foreground): the two files 20 passed in 12.67s -> 6.13s. Per test: the five 1.01s reap tests -> 0.22s each; stalled-remote 2.06s -> 1.04s; read-retry 0.32s -> 0.66s (three ready-gated spawns; determinism deliberately bought at +0.34s); slow-progress unchanged at ~2.07s. Three consecutive clean runs at 6.44s each, then three more under 12 saturating CPU spinners on an 18-core host: 7.61s / 7.10s / 7.64s, 20 passed every time.\n\nGATES: `make lint` PASS; `make typecheck` PASS (mypy, 582 source files); `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` -> `active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0`; `python scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py` -> clean; wider `pytest tests/unit/test_snapshot_fetch_stall_abort_12e4.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/` -> 508 passed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787206912395627001,"uuid":"950f2c9f-f540-4b65-a37e-689e33119291"}